        "title": "Fix clean script failure in common package",
        "summary": "The clean script in common/package.json now suppresses errors when removing tsconfig.tsbuildinfo. This prevents the script from failing if the file is already absent. Scope limited to the common package build tooling.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T15:19:16.062Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you tell the shared project toolkit to clean up its leftover build files, it used to crash if the progress file it was about to delete had already vanished on its own. Now the cleanup quietly continues if it simply has nothing to remove, so the tidy-up step no longer fails partway through. It affects anyone working inside the common package and who would notice the failure is gone.",
